<p id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">tableEvaluation of reasoning and answer traces under the same configuration as <span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tab.</span> <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ RAIN-Merging: A Gradient-Free Method to Enhance Instruction Following in Large Reasoning Models with Preserved Thinking Format" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We report Reasoning Internal Coherence (<span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RIC</span>) and Reasoning-Answer Alignment (<span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RAA</span>) on IFEval, AIME25, and GPQA (0-5 scale). The subsequent “<span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(relative gain)</span>” row reports the relative improvement of our method over the LRM, highlighted in green.


<span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:216.6pt;height:38.3pt;vertical-align:-17.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-66.9pt,11.8pt) scale(0.618152489652663,0.618152489652663) ;">
<span id="S4.SS2.fig2.2.2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
