</table>
</figure>
<div id="A9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For SFT, we use a batch size of 16 with the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2014</a>)</cite>, a learning rate of <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay of <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, and train for 20 epochs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For all model-merging methods (including the proposed RAIN-Merging and all baselines), we merge only the task vectors extracted from the ITM’s <math id="A9.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Q/K/V/O/FFN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>FFN</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Q/K/V/O/FFN}</annotation></semantics></math> modules. The specific hyperparameter settings for each baseline used in <span id="A9.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tab.</span> <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ RAIN-Merging: A Gradient-Free Method to Enhance Instruction Following in Large Reasoning Models with Preserved Thinking Format" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> are listed in <span id="A9.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tab.</span> <a href="#A9.T4" title="Table A4 ‣ I.3 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix I Detailed Experimental Setup ‣ RAIN-Merging: A Gradient-Free Method to Enhance Instruction Following in Large Reasoning Models with Preserved Thinking Format" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In <span id="A9.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RAIN-Merging</span>, we set the leakage penalty to <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=10</annotation></semantics></math> and bound the attention-head coefficients by <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tilde{\alpha}_{l},\tilde{\alpha}_{u}]=[0.0,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tilde{\alpha}_{l},\tilde{\alpha}_{u}]=[0.0,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>. The global scalar <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is selected via a grid search over <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.0,1.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.0,1.5]</annotation></semantics></math> with a step size of <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>; the chosen values for different model families are provided in <span id="A9.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tab.</span> <a href="#A9.T5" title="Table A5 ‣ I.3 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix I Detailed Experimental Setup ‣ RAIN-Merging: A Gradient-Free Method to Enhance Instruction Following in Large Reasoning Models with Preserved Thinking Format" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A5</span></a>. An ablation study of the global scalar <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is included in Appendix <a href="#A10.SS2" title="J.2 Ablation Study of the Global Scalar ‣ Appendix J Additional Experiments ‣ RAIN-Merging: A Gradient-Free Method to Enhance Instruction Following in Large Reasoning Models with Preserved Thinking Format" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
